[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Enemies/BossAddWaveResource.cs" id="3_wave"]

; The Iron King's fight, moved out of BossController's hard-coded table (Phase 28B) without changing
; a number: 66% / 33% thresholds, +25%/+15% then +30%/+20%, and the same ember flare burning hotter
; each stage. That equivalence is the point — it is what makes "no behaviour regression" something
; you can check rather than assert.
;
; He deliberately has NO enrage. Adding one would be a balance change wearing a refactor's clothes,
; and the first boss the player meets should be beatable at their own pace. The dragons carry the
; fuse instead.

; He does not fight alone past the first third. Two cinder thralls arrive when he is wounded, and
; from a third health his cultists keep coming — capped at three alive, so the phase applies pressure
; instead of accumulating into a wall. Both archetypes already exist and are faction.fallen; nothing
; here is invented for the occasion.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Wave_thralls"]
script = ExtResource("3_wave")
TemplateId = "enemy.cinder_thrall"
Count = 2
RepeatSeconds = 0.0
MaxAlive = 0
HealthMultiplier = 1.0

